Package: apx-stacks
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: apx,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: default apx stacks and package-manager definitions
 Stack and package-manager YAML definitions that let apx create subsystems
 based on other distributions. The base stacks and the package managers
 come from vanilla-apx-configs, the set Vanilla OS itself ships: Alpine,
 Arch Linux, Debian, Fedora, openSUSE, Ubuntu and Vanilla OS. The
 language-specific stacks, such as arch-go or ubuntu-python, come from
 apx-community.
 .
 Neither upstream provides a stack for Debian testing or unstable, so this
 package adds one of each.
